/**
	Whether the script set the voice of the voice, with set_voice or set_language, rather than the voice following the platform's own setting.
	bool tts_voice::voice_set;
	## Remarks:
		This property is read-only. Until the voice is set, the object speaks with the voice the platform's settings select, which it follows when the user changes them while the program runs: on Windows the default voice chosen in the system's speech settings; on Android the default voice, for the language chosen in the system's text-to-speech settings, of the engine preferred there, so changing the preferred engine, the language or the engine's own default voice changes it; on Apple platforms the voice chosen in the system's Spoken Content settings, or another voice of its language when that is a Siri voice, which apps can't use; on Linux the voice of Speech Dispatcher's configuration. It turns false again when refresh, called directly or by set_language, no longer finds the chosen voice, which was uninstalled for instance, and the object goes back to the voice the platform's settings select.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	tts_voice v;
	alert("Before", "voice_set: " + v.voice_set);
	v.set_voice(0);
	alert("After", "voice_set: " + v.voice_set);
}
